# Development Conventions

Follow @.agents/rules/development.md.

- Package manager: strictly `pnpm` (never npm or yarn).
- Validation: always run `pnpm test` and `pnpm build` after modifying code.
- Environment & Secrets: follow @.agents/rules/environment-and-security.md. Any new env variable requires security research and explicit confirmation from human author.
- Git: do not auto-commit changes. Only commit when explicitly requested.
- Production Deployment: `production/netlify` triggers live Netlify deployment. Never commit or merge feature branches directly to it; always merge into `main` first, then merge `main` into `production/netlify` to keep them in sync.
- TypeScript: strict mode enabled.
